notes: The owner explicitly requested V026 while V025 had not been separately accepted, so V025 is recorded as the previous version while the owner-confirmed passed baseline remains V024 / 0_2_4. V026 builds on V025 intersection/topology identity with an isolated deterministic two-intersection network experiment service: one enabled directed link selects an upstream/downstream pair, each intersection runs its own Fixed or Adaptive signal-controller instance, exogenous demand is shared between modes, and discharged upstream vehicles can enter a synthetic transfer pipeline and arrive downstream after the configured link travel time. Results include per-intersection waiting/queue/throughput/signal metrics, transfer-event evidence, network aggregate telemetry, persistence and CSV export. Cooperative neighbour-informed timing and emergency priority remain inactive. Physical/public-road traffic control remains disabled.
